    "title": "CBS Cancels Kate Walsh's New Sitcom 'The Tillbrooks' - Cupertino Today",
    "text": "Got story updates? Submit your updates here. ›The abrupt cancellation of a high-profile sitcom pilot signals strategic shifts in the network's comedy lineup.Cupertino TodayCBS has decided not to move forward with the comedy pilot 'The Tillbrooks', which starred Kate Walsh and Rhys Darby in the lead roles. The network made the decision as it finalizes its 2026-27 programming lineup, opting instead for a different comedy pilot that received stronger reception during network screenings. Why it matters The cancellation of 'The Tillbrooks' marks a significant shift in CBS's comedy strategy, as the network will now carry only three half-hour series next season, down from four this year. This decision reflects the broader changes happening at CBS parent company Paramount Global following its recent acquisition by Skydance. The details The Tillbrooks, formerly known as Regency, was a multi-camera sitcom created by Tara Hernandez and produced by Warner Bros TV. The pilot did not perform as well as another comedy pilot during network screenings last week, leading CBS to pass on the project. With the cancellation of freshman comedy DMV earlier this cycle and the ending of veteran sitcom The Neighborhood, CBS will have only two returning half-hour series - the single-camera Ghosts and the multi-camera Georgie & Mandy's First Marriage - on its comedy slate next season. CBS made the decision to cancel The Tillbrooks as it finalizes its 2026-27 programming lineup.The network will officially reveal its full 2026-27 schedule next week. The players Kate WalshAn American actress known for her roles in shows like Grey's Anatomy and Private Practice.Rhys DarbyA New Zealand actor and comedian who has appeared in numerous TV shows and films, including Flight of the Conchords and Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle.Tara HernandezThe creator of The Tillbrooks pilot.Warner Bros TVThe production company behind The Tillbrooks.Paramount GlobalThe parent company of CBS, which recently completed its acquisition by Skydance. Got photos? Submit your photos here. › What’s next CBS will officially reveal its full 2026-27 programming lineup next week, including the three comedy series it will carry next season. The takeaway The cancellation of Kate Walsh's new sitcom 'The Tillbrooks' is a significant shift in CBS's comedy strategy, as the network trims its half-hour series lineup amid broader changes at parent company Paramount Global. This decision highlights the challenges of developing and maintaining a successful comedy slate in the evolving television landscape.",
